# HookSwap per-chain RPC config  (COMMITTED TEMPLATE — no keys, and none are needed)
#
# Copy to  config/rpc.env  (gitignored) if you want to override anything, then `source` it (or pass
# via docker --env-file) alongside .env when running the adapter and/or routing-api.
#
# Convention: WEB3_RPC_<chainId>  — this is what BOTH the routing-api fork and this adapter's
# embed-SOR mode read (see src/chains.ts `rpcEnvVar`, and routing-api/hookswap/README.md §1).
#
# PUBLIC RPCs ONLY — NO ALCHEMY, NO INFURA, NO HOSTED KEYS
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   2026-08-02 (Reggie): HookSwap's single hosted (Alchemy) key went over quota and returned HTTP 429
#   on EVERY chain simultaneously, which took down all chain reads. The stack now runs on public
#   endpoints with up to 5 auto-fallbacks per chain.
#
#   Each WEB3_RPC_<chainId> accepts EITHER one URL or a COMMA-SEPARATED, ORDERED list. Requests try
#   index 0, fail over to the next on error, and wrap around; a failing endpoint is skipped for a 60s
#   cooldown. See src/rpc.ts for the failover contract.
#
#   You normally do NOT need to set any of these: src/chains.ts already carries the ordered,
#   live-tested public list for every chain. Setting one REPLACES the built-in list for that chain,
#   so include your fallbacks in the same comma-separated value.
#
# ⛔ NEVER use these — they answer HTTP 200 with WRONG data (hard-filtered by src/rpc.ts anyway):
#      https://megaeth.blockscout.com/api/eth-rpc          silently drops logs, caps results at 1000
#      https://robinhood.drpc.org                          "does not exist" on every method but eth_chainId
#      https://robinhoodchain.blockscout.com/api/eth-rpc   HTTP 429 as result:null with no error field
#      https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com         403 on eth_getLogs and archive eth_call
#
# ⚠️ Keep each value on its own line with NO trailing inline comment: systemd's EnvironmentFile does
#    NOT strip inline `# ...` (unlike dotenv), so `URL   # note` becomes part of the URL and breaks
#    the provider. This bit us for real once (CLAUDE.md 2026-07-07).

# MegaETH (4326)
# WEB3_RPC_4326=https://mainnet.megaeth.com/rpc,https://megaeth.drpc.org,https://4326.rpc.thirdweb.com

# Robinhood (4663) — ONLY ONE public endpoint works; there is NO failover on this chain.
# WEB3_RPC_4663=https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com

# Ink (57073)
# WEB3_RPC_57073=https://ink.gateway.tenderly.co,https://rpc-qnd.inkonchain.com,https://ink.drpc.org,https://rpc-gel.inkonchain.com,https://57073.rpc.thirdweb.com

# XLayer (196) — the last two cap eth_getLogs at 100 blocks, hence the order.
# WEB3_RPC_196=https://xlayer.drpc.org,https://196.rpc.thirdweb.com,https://rpc.xlayer.tech,https://xlayerrpc.okx.com

# HyperEVM (999) — the OFFICIAL endpoint is last on purpose (it rate-limits aggressively).
# WEB3_RPC_999=https://hyperliquid.drpc.org,https://rpc.hyperlend.finance,https://hyperliquid.rpc.blxrbdn.com,https://hyperliquid-json-rpc.stakely.io,https://999.rpc.thirdweb.com,https://rpc.hyperliquid.xyz/evm

# Tempo (4217)
# WEB3_RPC_4217=https://rpc.tempo.xyz,https://rpc.mainnet.tempo.xyz,https://tempo.drpc.org

# Stable (988) — the last two cap eth_getLogs at 500 blocks.
# WEB3_RPC_988=https://stable-mainnet.rpc.sentio.xyz,https://rpc.stable.xyz,https://stable.drpc.org

# Sepolia (11155111)
# WEB3_RPC_11155111=https://sepolia.drpc.org,https://sepolia.gateway.tenderly.co,https://11155111.rpc.thirdweb.com
